From: lancethepants <lancethepants@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mt76: connac: set VHT phy mode on 2.4GHz

With vendor 256-QAM (0204/0205) a 2.4GHz station can be VHT, and the
rate control TLV then carries MODE_VHT and a VHT MCS set, but the phy
mode never included AC on 2.4GHz. On mt7986 the firmware answered the
mismatch by sending to the station at 6 Mbit/s OFDM.

Set PHY_MODE_AC / PHY_TYPE_BIT_VHT on 2.4GHz when VHT is supported.
Without vendor_vht_2g nothing on 2.4GHz has vht_supported, so this is a
no-op there.

---
--- a/mt76_connac_mcu.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mcu.c
@@ -820,6 +820,10 @@
 		if (ht_cap->ht_supported)
 			mode |= PHY_TYPE_BIT_HT;
 
+		/* vendor 256-QAM: VHT on 2.4 GHz */
+		if (vht_cap->vht_supported)
+			mode |= PHY_TYPE_BIT_VHT;
+
 		if (he_cap && he_cap->has_he)
 			mode |= PHY_TYPE_BIT_HE;
 
@@ -1353,6 +1357,10 @@
 		if (ht_cap->ht_supported)
 			mode |= PHY_MODE_GN;
 
+		/* vendor 256-QAM: VHT on 2.4 GHz */
+		if (vht_cap->vht_supported)
+			mode |= PHY_MODE_AC;
+
 		if (he_cap && he_cap->has_he)
 			mode |= PHY_MODE_AX_24G;
 	} else if (band == NL80211_BAND_5GHZ) {
